      "content": "so if we look at the actual outcomes, doesn't it seem like the \"capital flight\" argument is mostly used to avoid the conversation about redistribution? like, if a country has the right regulations in place, isn't the most logical and beneficial conclusion that a wealth tax is the best way to fix the widening gap between the rich and everyone else?",
